From 2aa5d966cd5d9d53d6288d0c8144ebe7afec792a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:23:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.8: amaspark - with MLO the carriers are one link set;
 raise all of it

Field, RT-BE96U, mld_enable=1: parking wl0 took wl1 and wl2 down with it (the
backhaul MLO link set), the daemon saw them already down, treated them as not
its own, and a release raised only wl0 - leaving the 5 and 6 GHz carriers down
with parking off. Every client network on every band stayed up throughout.

The daemon now snapshots every primary before it acts, claims any that
dropped alongside (logged as a linked drop, 6 GHz included - the driver's
doing, not ours), and raises the whole set on release. With MLO off nothing
changes: the radios park and release independently and 6 GHz is never
touched. Both worlds exercised in a host simulation around the real file.
RWIF_86 reworded to say so (25 dicts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
