 RWIF_85=AiMesh backhaul parking
-RWIF_86=With no mesh node paired, the hidden AiMesh backhaul network still beacons on every band and accepts connections with a key you never chose. Parking takes the 2.4 and 5 GHz carriers off the air until you search for or add a node, then puts them back; if the search ends without a node they park again. 6 GHz is never touched: its carrier shares the beacon your main network rides on. Every park and release is written to the system log with its reason.
+RWIF_86=With no mesh node paired, the hidden AiMesh backhaul network still beacons on every band and accepts connections with a key you never chose. Parking takes the 2.4 and 5 GHz carriers off the air until you search for or add a node, then puts them back; if the search ends without a node they park again. With MLO enabled the three carriers form one link set and go down and come back together, 6 GHz included; your own networks on every band stay up throughout. Every park and release is written to the system log with its reason.
 RWIF_87=Park the backhaul while no node is paired
 RWIF_88=Parking is on
 RWIF_89=Parking is off
